    "display_name": "Book Reviews",
    "long_instructions": "You are building a classifier to determine if a book review is positive or negative.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n\r\nComplete the implementation of `get_features`. `get_features` accepts text as input and returns a bag-of-words representation of the text: in other words, it returns a dictionary mapping words to how frequently they appear in the text.\r\n\r\nYour function should:\r\n\r\n- Tokenize text using the provided `tokenize` helper function. `tokenize` accepts a string as input and returns a list of lowercased tokens.\r\n- Compute a dictionary where the keys are each of the tokens in the text and the values are the number of times each token appears. For example, if the input text is “The cat saw the dog”, your function should return `{\"cat\": 1,\"dog\": 1, \"saw\": 1, \"the\": 2}`.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nYou can use a `for` loop over the list of tokens you get back from the `tokenize` function. Consider: what should your loop do when you encounter a new token? What should you do when it encounters a token that it’s seen before?",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Build a classifier to determine if a book review is positive or negative.",
    "thumbnail_url": "https://images.code.org/3dbbf6546c3179125eaadbcb6c05312c-stack-of-books.png",
